-- title:
--   Base change of the chart-vanishing criterion along a field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, $n$ a natural number, $Z$ a scheme and $\iota : Z \to \operatorname{Proj} k[x_0,\dots ,x_n]$ an affine morphism to the $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded ring of homogeneous components of `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) k`; let $K$ be a field with a $k$-algebra structure, $Z'$ a scheme and $\iota' : Z' \to \operatorname{Proj} K[x_0,\dots ,x_n]$ an affine morphism, and let $e : Z' \to Z$ be a morphism such that the square formed by $e$, $\iota'$ followed by `ProjSpace.π K n`, $\iota$ followed by `ProjSpace.π k n` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $k \to K$ is a pullback, and such that $e$ followed by $\iota$ equals $\iota'$ followed by the base-change morphism $\operatorname{Proj} K[x] \to \operatorname{Proj} k[x]$ induced by the degree-preserving ring map `MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap k K)`. Let $m$ be a natural number and $J$ an ideal of $k[x_0,\dots ,x_n]$ stable under taking homogeneous components of its elements, and assume: for every $d \ge m$ and every $F$ homogeneous of degree $d$, $F \in J$ if and only if for each $i$ the image under $\iota^{\sharp}$ on the basic open $D_+(x_i)$ of the section attached to the homogeneous localisation class $F/x_i^{d}$ vanishes. The conclusion is the same equivalence over $K$: for every $d \ge m$ and every $F$ in $K[x_0,\dots ,x_n]$ homogeneous of degree $d$, $F$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of $J$ under `MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap k K)` if and only if for each $i$ the image under $\iota'^{\sharp}$ on $D_+(x_i)$ of the section attached to $F/x_i^{d}$ vanishes.
--
--   This is the flat base change statement for the chart-vanishing dictionary: the property that, in degrees $\ge m$, a homogeneous ideal is exactly the set of forms whose affine chart classes pull back to zero on $Z$ is inherited by the extended ideal on any realisation of the base change of $Z$ to a field extension. It feeds the analysis of Hilbert functions of points in `AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_ProjSpace_mem_map_iff_forall_app_awayToSection_eq_zero_of_baseChange_field.lean

